Content lines are now unfolded on the encoded byte stream before decoding,
so a fold point inside a multi-byte UTF-8 character (for example a CJK
character or an emoji) no longer corrupts the value. In strict mode,
illegal folds, bare carriage returns, unclosed quotes and invalid UTF-8
raise a ``ParseError`` carrying the offset of the problem; lenient mode
keeps its established tolerance. Quoted parameter tokens are now matched
as exactly one pair of double quotes.
